User Management API Documentation

1. Overview

The User Management API allows applications to retrieve user information.

This is a fictional API created for learning purposes.

2. API Endpoint

"GET /api/v1/users/{user_id}"

This endpoint retrieves information about a specific user.

3. Request Parameter

Parameter| Type| Description
user_id| Integer| The unique ID of the user

4. Example Request

GET /api/v1/users/25

5. Example Response

{
  "id": 25,
  "name": "John",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "status": "active"
}

6. Response Fields

- "id": The user's unique identification number.
- "name": The user's full name.
- "email": The user's email address.
- "status": The current status of the account.

7. HTTP Status Codes

- "200": Request successful.
- "400": Invalid request.
- "401": Authentication required.
- "404": User not found.
- "500": Internal server error.

8. Conclusion

The User Management API provides a simple way for applications to retrieve user information.
